      "writtenOn": "2015-12-17T15:07:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think making it disabled by default is not necessary here.\n\nThis really is a kill switch, and I debated even putting it in.  Since no implied roles are defined by default,  there is no change in behavior by default; enabling the is will do nothing.\n\nIn the future, we may decide that we want to expand roles in the policy file as opposed to in the token, to minimize transfer size.  If that is the case, then we can disable this here as well.\n\n\nDisabling implied roles will  prevent people from being able to use the feature if it is disabled by default, delaying adoption. Is that wise.",
